WEBVTT

00:00:00.431 --> 00:00:04.002
Window functions solve a different analytical problem from GROUP BY.

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:07.332
GROUP BY collapses many input rows into one row per group.

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:12.242
A window function usually keeps the original detail rows and adds analytical context beside them.

00:00:12.242 --> 00:00:19.352
For example, we can keep every employee row while adding a department rank or department average.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:24.067
PARTITION BY defines groups for the window calculation, while ORDER BY inside OVER can define ranking or

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:29.422
running sequence. This is powerful because you do not have to choose between detail and summary.

00:00:29.422 --> 00:00:31.302
You can display both in the same result.

00:00:31.302 --> 00:00:36.372
When deciding between GROUP BY and a window function, ask whether you want to collapse rows or keep them

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:43.067
visible. Window functions calculate across related rows without collapsing them.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:47.692
That lets you keep row-level detail while adding rank, running totals, or group averages.

00:00:47.692 --> 00:00:52.422
Always define the partition and ordering carefully because those clauses describe which rows belong together

00:00:52.422 --> 00:00:54.278
and in what sequence.
